MVSTMP(1)                      ZOAU Command Syntax                     MVSTMP(1)

NAME

	mvstmp - Generate a valid MVS dataset name suitable for use as a
	temporary dataset.

SYNOPSIS

	mvstmp [-cdhv] [PREFIX]

	-c
		Runs a test to verify if the current user is able to write to a
		temporary dataset using the provided or default PREFIX.

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

	-v
		Print out verbose command information.

DESCRIPTION

	Generate a name suitable for use as a z/OS dataset name and write
	the name to stdout. No dataset is actually created - this utility
	just generates a name.

	If the PREFIX argument or TMPHLQ environment variables are used, the
	value provided must adhere to the following rules:

	* It must be a maximum of 17 characters long.
	* It must follow z/OS dataset naming rules.
	* It may contain 0 or more periods. For example the following prefixes
	  are valid: ZOAU, ZOAU.PREFIX, ZOAU.PREFIX.NAME

	The generated name is of the format:
		<PREFIX>.<PROCESS>.<TIMESTAMP>.<COUNTER>

	The name components are as follows:

	<PREFIX>
		Defaults to the current user ID if no prefix is specified.
		Overrides TMPHLQ environment variable if provided.
		Prefix must conform to MVS dataset naming conventions.

	<PROCESS>
		'P' followed by the low order 7 digits of the process ID
		of the mvstmp process.

	<TIMESTAMP>
		'T' followed by the low order 7 digits of the microseconds
		component of the current time of day.

	<COUNTER>
		'C' followed by 7 zeros.

	For example:

		PREFIX00.Pnnnnnnn.Tnnnnnnn.C0000000

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

	TMPHLQ
		Set the value used as PREFIX in the temporary dataset name.

EXAMPLES

	Generate a temporary dataset name with a high-level qualifier (HLQ) of TEST:

		mvstmp TEST

	Generate a temporary dataset name with a high-level qualifier of ZOAU.PREFIX

		mvstmp ZOAU.PREFIX

	Generate a temporary dataset name with a high-level qualifier of ZOAU,
	while using the environment variable TMPHLQ:

		export TMPHLQ="ZOAU"; mvstmp

	Check if the current user ID is able to write to the high-level qualifier
	ZOAUTEST:

		mvstmp -c ZOAUTEST

EXIT VALUES

	0
		mvstmp completed without error.

	1
		The environment variable __POSIX_TMPNAM could not be set to "NO".

	2
		Syntax error.  Correct the mvstmp invocation and rerun the command.

	3
		Invalid PREFIX value. Ensure that the dataset name prefix conforms to
		the rules specified in the DESCRIPTION section of this page.

	4
		Write test failed. mvstmp was unable to perform a test write to the
		generated dataset name. Correct the PREFIX value or contact your system
		programmer to adjust the permissions of the invoking user ID.

	5
		PREFIX is too long.  Reduce the length of the prefix string.

	non-zero
		mvstmp failed. See error messages for details.
